  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 300 AM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nThe nice fall weather looks to continue through Monday across\ncentral and southeast IL, favorable weather for harvesting and\noutdoor activities.\n\nThe 08Z/3 am surface map shows 1032 mb high pressure over the\nsouthern Quebec Province and ridging sw into IL/IN. Aloft there\nis an upper level ridge over the nations mid section with cutoff\nlow/trofs off the mid Atlantic/New England coast and off the\nCalifornia coast. A weak short wave trof was over the\nCentral Plains in central KS and producing isolated to scattered\nshowers over the Central Plains, as far east as far western MO\nand far sw Iowa. Broken to overcast mid/high clouds were\nspreading into sw Iowa and central/western MO while nearly clear\nskies prevail over IL. Some patchy shallow ground fog over far\neastern IL near Wabash and Kankakee river valleys and over\nShawnee National forest in southern IL. Patchy fog over far\neastern/se CWA to lift quickly by mid morning. Temps were \nmostly in the 40s over CWA, but as cool as 39F at NWS Lincoln \nand Robinson, with BMI the milder spot at 49F. \n\nThe short wave trof over the Central Plains will weaken as it\nmoves over the MO valley today, spreading some mid/high clouds\neastward into mainly western/sw CWA today with a fair amount of\nsunshine overall today especially in eastern IL. Surface high \npressure ridge remains over IL keeping light to calm winds along\nwith dry low levels. Highs today in the low to mid 70s which is\nabout 10 degrees warmer than normal. Fair skies tonight with\nlows in the mid to upper 40s. 1030 mb or stronger high pressure\nover western Quebec and ridging into IL on Thu to continue ample\nsunshine with light ne winds and highs in the mid 70s. Light SE\nflow on Friday with a fair amount of sunshine and highs in the\nlow to mid 70s (coolest near the Indiana border).  \n\nMedium range models continue to build a strong 500 mb ridge into\nIL Fri/Sat as 500 mb heights rise to 588 decameters or higher by\nSat afternoon. SSE winds Saturday and more SW on Sunday but\nstill fairly light flow especially Sunday. Skies become partly\nsunny over central IL during Sat with mostly sunny skies in SE\nIL and highs in the mid 70s (upper 70s from SPI sw). Partly\ncloudy skies prevail Sat night through Monday overall. Highs\n75-80F on Sunday and low to mid 70s Monday.  \n\nForecast models diverge with upper level trof moving into the\nCentral Plains on Monday and pushing a frontal boundary se into\nIL Monday night into Tue. This could bring our next chance of \nshowers to the area overnight Mon night into Tue, though NBM\npops are currently 20% or less and mainly on Tuesday. Strong\nupper level ridge over the Southeast States early next work week\ncould slow this frontal boundary and also return gulf flow\nlimited by surface high pressure over mid Atlantic and gulf\ncoast states. Temperatures to cool closer to normal for middle \nof next week starting on Tuesday. A stronger system appears to \nbring a better chance of showers to IL middle of next week \naround Wed night and Thu with temperatures cooling further.",
